    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2LUVdS2HhkPxfyzVVQAEeL1)_\n\nTwo modules differed from what their docs tangle to on `main`. The docs are authoritative, so the `.el` files follow them:\n\n- **`sp-org-tag-groups.el`**: the committed file had the old `sp-org-tag-group-of` and no `sp-org-tag-groups--explicit-groups`, which the new `sp-org-tag-group-of` calls, so any tag lookup would signal a void function. Re-tangled.\n- **`sp-org-custom-highlight`**: the doc renamed the command to `sp-org-insert-inline-comment` but still bound `C-c h` to `my-org-insert-inline-comment`. The doc binding now uses the new name; the `.el` is re-tangled.\n\nThe third difference on `main`, `sp-search.el`, is fixed in #253.\n\n`tools/check-tangle.sh` shows no difference for these two modules in Emacs 29.3 batch. Not run in the interactive config.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCstZCQ3so9WszzwkT\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
